# XSH setegid()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Appropriate privileges are implementation-defined (XBD 3.21). Each test
# runs in a child of a privileged test process and first probes, in a
# disposable process and the setup phase, a call that only a privileged
# process may make (setegid() to a group ID the process does not hold);
# the test is UNRESOLVED when the probe does not show the state the
# assertion needs. A process loses appropriate privileges here by setting
# its user IDs to 65534 in the setup phase. Group IDs used: 65534 and
# 65533 (given to the process), 65532 (probes), 65531 (refused targets).

assertion  XSH.setegid.001
anchor     functions/setegid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/setegid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       With appropriate privileges and all group IDs 0, setegid(65534)
           returns 0, getegid() then returns 65534 and getgid() still 0.
needs      root
note       The saved set-group-ID equals the real group ID here, so whether
           it changed cannot be seen; XSH.setegid.002 checks it.
nomutant   no fault is planted in a call that changes the process IDs (reviewed by hand against the text; see docs/methodology.md)
test       t/001-privileged.c

assertion  XSH.setegid.002
anchor     functions/setegid.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       A process without appropriate privileges with real group ID
           65534 and effective and saved set-group-ID 65533: setegid(65534)
           returns 0 with getegid() and getgid() 65534, and setegid(65533)
           (the saved set-group-ID, still 65533) then returns 0 with
           getegid() 65533 and getgid() 65534.
needs      root
note       setregid() (XSI) sets the IDs apart, so the test runs only on
           XSI systems; the requirement itself is not XSI.
nomutant   no fault is planted in a call that changes the process IDs (reviewed by hand against the text; see docs/methodology.md)
test       t/002-unprivileged.c

assertion  XSH.setegid.003
anchor     functions/setegid.html#ERRORS/EPERM
anchor     functions/setegid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       A process without appropriate privileges with real and saved
           set-group-ID 0 and effective group ID 65533 gets -1 with EPERM
           from setegid(65531), and getegid() is still 65533.
needs      root
nomutant   no fault is planted in a call that changes the process IDs (reviewed by hand against the text; see docs/methodology.md)
test       t/003-eperm.c

assertion  XSH.setegid.004
anchor     functions/setegid.html#ERRORS/EPERM
class      required
since      2001
says       The same process gets -1 with EPERM from setegid(65533): its
           current effective group ID is neither its real group ID nor its
           saved set-group-ID, which are the only values allowed without
           privileges.
needs      root
nomutant   no fault is planted in a call that changes the process IDs (reviewed by hand against the text; see docs/methodology.md)
test       t/004-eperm-effective.c

assertion  XSH.setegid.005
anchor     functions/setegid.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap03.html#3.165
class      required
since      2001
says       With appropriate privileges, setegid((gid_t)-1) returns -1 with
           EINVAL ((gid_t)-1 is never a valid group ID) and getegid() stays
           0.
needs      root
nomutant   no fault is planted in a call that changes the process IDs (reviewed by hand against the text; see docs/methodology.md)
test       t/005-einval.c

assertion  XSH.setegid.006
anchor     functions/setegid.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With appropriate privileges and the supplementary group list set
           to {65534}, setegid(65533) leaves the supplementary list
           unchanged: what getgroups() reports, leaving out the effective
           group ID before and after (which it may include), is the same.
needs      root
note       The list is set with pc_drop_groups() (setgroups(), not in
           POSIX, where the system has it); without a supplementary group
           the test is UNRESOLVED.
nomutant   no fault is planted in a call that changes the process IDs (reviewed by hand against the text; see docs/methodology.md)
test       t/006-groups.c

assertion  XSH.setegid.007
anchor     functions/setegid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.9
class      required
since      2001
says       When one thread of a privileged process calls setegid(65534),
           another thread of the process then gets 65534 from getegid().
needs      root
nomutant   no fault is planted in a call that changes the process IDs (reviewed by hand against the text; see docs/methodology.md)
test       t/007-threads.c
